intro='''<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Garrison 0.7.5 building review</title><style>body{font:17px/1.55 system-ui;margin:30px auto;max-width:1320px;padding:0 24px;background:#f4f2eb;color:#252a32}h1,h2{line-height:1.2}section{background:white;padding:24px;margin:26px 0;border:1px solid #ddd}img{max-width:100%;height:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}td,th{padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;text-align:left}a{color:#145b9b}nav{display:flex;gap:18px;flex-wrap:wrap}.note{background:#fff2d1;padding:18px}</style><h1>Seven Vietnamese buildings · candidate 0.7.5</h1><p class="note">Independent provisional source-art review. None reaches the requested 9/10 threshold. Owner colour, native appearance, construction, destruction, repair, access and production require the final candidate test. Successful native cooking and exact resource preservation do not establish those native gates.</p><p>Baseline scores are the user's previous subjective review; the current five-criterion subtotal is normalized over 90% because functional owner colour cannot be scored offline. The full rubric remains incomplete. This is not a claim that the prior review used the same scoring method.</p>'''
